{"ts": 1791255131.83684, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "notes_read", "args": {"note_id": "writeup"}, "output": "# Week 3 build\n\n## What I built\n(todo)\n\n## Environment definition\nI listed state and actions already, see below.\nState: files, calendar. Actions: open, send.\n\n## Evaluation\n(todo)\n", "t": 4, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.3897489112518813, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255132.9316769, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Good start. Let\u2019s tighten the environment definition so it matches the build prompt. You already have state and actions; we still need observations, dynamics, and a clear note about any hidden variable / partial observability if relevant. After that, we\u2019ll add the evaluation section with pass^k on at least 3 seeds. If you want, send me what you think the observations and dynamics are in your system, and I\u2019ll help refine them.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=4 messages 2m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.4578672350207063, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255134.474257, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 for a POMDP, the short answer is: the agent does not observe the full state directly, so it must act based on observations and an internal belief about the hidden state. In your build, if attention matters, treat attention as part of the hidden state: you can\u2019t directly see it perfectly, but it affects what the student learns from the same visible inputs.\n\nA clean one-liner you can use:\n\n\u201cBecause the student\u2019s true attention is not fully observable, the environment is partially observable: the agent receives observations (e.g., messages, readings, quiz results) and must infer a belief over hidden state variables such as attention/fatigue.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pomdp\n[activity] t=6 messages 1m", "t": 7, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.46371272055594026, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.47644044389342016, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255136.4013638, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Absolutely \u2014 here\u2019s the direct answer you can use:\n\n**POMDP answer:** The environment is partially observable because the agent cannot directly see the full true state. In this build, the student\u2019s hidden attention/fatigue is a hidden state variable. The agent only sees observations like messages, readings, and quiz results, so it must act using those observations and an internal belief about the hidden state. Measuring attention is itself an action that may have a cost.\n\nIf you want a paste-ready version for the write-up:\n\n\u201cFriday\u2019s build is a POMDP because the agent does not observe the full underlying state directly. In particular, student attention and fatigue are hidden variables: the agent only receives observations such as messages, reading completion, and quiz performance, and must infer a belief over the true state. Some actions, like checking attention or giving a quiz, can be used to reduce uncertainty but have a cost.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pomdp\n[activity] t=7 messages 1m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 7, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.4680982448588208, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.5564404438934202, "persistence": 0.3721403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255137.536242, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the direct answer again, in paste-ready form:\n\n**POMDP:** The environment is partially observable because the agent cannot directly see the full underlying state. In this build, student attention/fatigue can be treated as hidden state variables. The agent only observes things like messages, reading completion, and quiz results, so it must infer a belief about the true state from those observations. Actions like checking attention or giving a quiz can reduce uncertainty, but they have a cost.\n\nIf you want, I can also help you turn that into a 2\u20133 sentence write-up for your draft.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=8 messages 1m", "t": 9, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.6364404438934201, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255138.592797, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## POMDP\nThis build can be modeled as a POMDP because the agent cannot directly observe the full true state. The hidden state includes variables like student attention and fatigue. The agent only receives observations such as messages, reading completion, and quiz results, so it must act using a belief over the hidden state. Some actions, such as checking attention or giving a quiz, can reduce uncertainty but may have a cost.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 9, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.6364404438934201, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255139.523577, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "Attention as a hidden variable"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 9, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.6364404438934201, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255139.525996, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "pass@k vs pass^k"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 9, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.6364404438934201, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255140.8466601, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick check: do you want me to write the evaluation section for you now? If so, the key point is: use **pass^k**, not pass@k. That means you report whether **all k runs succeed** for each seed, and you need it for **at least 3 seeds**. If you want, I can draft the exact paragraph and append it to your write-up.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k", "t": 11, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.35645686063509857}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.6564404438934202, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255142.2849832, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the direct answer you can use:\n\n**pass^k** means you run the build k times and it counts as a success only if **all k runs succeed**. It\u2019s a reliability metric: it answers \u201chow often does the system work every time?\u201d rather than \u201cdid at least one run work?\u201d\n\nFor your build, the requirement is to report **pass^k on at least 3 seeds**.\n\nPaste-ready version:\n\n\u201cEvaluation uses pass^k: for each seed, we run the build k times and count it as successful only if all k runs succeed. This measures reliability, which is the relevant deployment criterion. We report pass^k for at least 3 seeds.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=11 messages 1m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 11, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.3619527777570664}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.7364404438934201, "persistence": 0.31214034943975877, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255143.382803, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is:\n\n**pass^k** means the build counts as successful only if **all k runs succeed**. It\u2019s a stricter reliability measure than pass@k.\n\nFor your write-up, you can say:\n\n\u201cpass^k reports whether all k repeated runs succeed; for this build, we report pass^k on at least 3 seeds.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=12 idle 1m", "t": 13, "activity": [{"t": 12, "app": "idle", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.3619527777570664}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8458151230937745, "motivation": 0.494715486329607, "reliance": 0.7364404438934201, "persistence": 0.31214034943975877, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 1.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255144.240906, "type": "step", "step": 32, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## Evaluation\nWe report **pass^k** on at least 3 seeds. pass^k means the build is counted as successful only if **all k runs succeed** for a given seed, so it measures reliability rather than just occasional success.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 13, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.47273975115056244, "pass_k": 0.3619527777570664}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8458151230937745, "motivation": 0.494715486329607, "reliance": 0.7364404438934201, "persistence": 0.31214034943975877, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 1.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": []}}
